   "notes": "63-66 Bridge Street: early-19th-century pink-washed stucco block with a curved corner, ruled ashlar lines, white band course under the second floor, multi-pane sashes, first-floor windows with scrolled console hoods, deep dentil cornice; maroon Hardy's sweetshop front with door at the corner and charcoal crepe-cafe front. This is the St John's Street side south of the curve; bay count inferred from Commons '63-65 Bridge Street, Cambridge.jpg' and the left edge of '14 And 15, St John's Street.jpg'."
